WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.720
I'm starting today with something that is the&nbsp;
perfect nexus of ignorance and nationalism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:12.960
I think is the way I would put it, the unhinged&nbsp;
nationalism, in fact, of some of the new Trumpy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:17.840
and members of Congress really knows no bounds.&nbsp;
And it even now is being applied to American&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:23.440
territories whose residents are citizens of the&nbsp;
United States. And I'm talking about none other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:30.560
than radical, outrageous, disgusting, depraved and&nbsp;
delusional. Congresswoman Marjorie Taylor Green,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:39.680
of course, of Jewish space laser fame, she said at&nbsp;
a side panel, a sort of breakout session at CPAC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:46.480
a couple of weeks ago, that American taxpayer&nbsp;
money shouldn't go to foreign countries like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:53.760
wait for it, Guam. Now, Guam is, of course,&nbsp;
an American territory. The people of Guam are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.960
American citizens. The reason it took us a couple&nbsp;
of weeks to hear about this, even though CPAC was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:04.960
a couple of weeks ago, is that it was at one of&nbsp;
these breakout sessions. So what we watched on TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.600
from CPAC, that wasn't all. They also had breakout&nbsp;
sessions with smaller groups where a lot of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.120
things I said were even nuttier and even more&nbsp;
ignorant, if you can imagine that it was filmed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:19.280
Here is Marjorie Taylor Green saying no&nbsp;
more money for foreign countries like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:26.080
Guam, where everybody's an American citizen.
And I wanted to take my regular person, normal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:32.800
everyday American values, which is we love our&nbsp;
country. We believe our hard earned tax dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:47.760
should just go for America, not for what China,&nbsp;
Russia, the middle class. If we want to put money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:54.240
into schools, if we want to build a border wall,&nbsp;
we want it right here at home, no more money&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.480
for foreign countries like Guam.
This reminded me, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.640
and I think it reminded many, many others&nbsp;
of the whole Puerto Ricans should go back to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.440
their country. Puerto Ricans, of course, are&nbsp;
American. There is no country to go back to.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:14.400
It's part of the United States. And on a serious&nbsp;
note, this really does reinforce the importance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:22.480
normalizing the status of places like Puerto Rico&nbsp;
and Guam and others. Green, as an elected official&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:28.720
should know what is part of the United States and&nbsp;
what is not. But this is also another reminder, as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:34.080
if we needed one, that the way we deal with Puerto&nbsp;
Rico and Guam and others like American Samoa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.720
it really makes no sense. In many ways. We do&nbsp;
treat them as if they are foreign countries.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:44.080
There are different statuses for different&nbsp;
territories. People born on American Samoa,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:50.480
for example, are U.S. nationals, but they're not&nbsp;
U.S. citizens. People from Puerto Rico and Guam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:56.720
are U.S. citizens at birth. It's a mess and it&nbsp;
needs to be fixed. But what foreign country does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:03.600
she think Guam is anyway? Now, Marjorie Taylor&nbsp;
Green is a moron. Yes, she has no business being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:09.120
in the House of Representatives. And this proves&nbsp;
that there needs to be serious consideration given&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.720
to the status of overseas territories. She's&nbsp;
in Congress. She should know, without a doubt.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:23.040
But the truth is, if you ask your average person&nbsp;
in the street, is Guam its own country or a U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.160
territory, many people would have no idea. This&nbsp;
isn't completely unique to the United States. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.760
think if you go to the UK and you ask people about&nbsp;
some of the more obscure British territories,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:40.640
I think many people in the UK also wouldn't know.&nbsp;
But the issue is people in government should know.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.960
And these territories, as far as the U.S. is&nbsp;
concerned, do not have adequate representation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:53.840
in their own government. So it's particularly&nbsp;
it's a it's a vicious cycle when they don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.880
have adequate representation. And then our elected&nbsp;
officials sometimes don't even know that they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:02.000
lacking the representation because they don't&nbsp;
even know that it's part of the United States&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.680
unless it's convenient for some&nbsp;
other reason. Like, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:14.320
when Republicans want to talk about how bad a job&nbsp;
a Democratic president is doing on controlling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:22.880
North Korea, they will say North Korea could hit&nbsp;
U.S. territories with missiles like Guam, then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:27.760
it's convenient. Then all of a sudden they figure&nbsp;
out Guam is a U.S. territory. There are many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:33.840
Americans who don't realize Puerto Rico's part of&nbsp;
the US. Puerto Ricans are U.S. citizens. There are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.240
some Americans who think New Mexico is part of&nbsp;
Mexico rather than a US state. There's plenty of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:44.400
ignorance to go around, but Marjorie Taylor Green&nbsp;
is an elected official and it's very politically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:50.480
relevant. So just another confirmation that she&nbsp;
has no business, no business whatsoever serving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:56.720
in government. And hopefully she will either not&nbsp;
run for reelection in 2022 or be voted out in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.080
bloodbath election. Let's hope for the latter.&nbsp;
I think it would be more more entertaining.

